            <ArticleTitle>[Neuropathies following hand surgery under supraclavicular plexus anesthesia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>15-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>15 cases with pain in the shoulder girdle following an operation in supraclavicular brachial plexus anesthesia are reported. The pain developped after an interval of several days. According to the neurological findings the diagnosis is regarded as neuralgic amyotrophy. Possible causes are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
